<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="utf-8" />
        <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
        <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
        <title>Instructions | Pathfinder Critical Hits & Fumbles</title>
        <link
            href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=MedievalSharp&family=Crimson+Text:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;1,400&display=swap"
            rel="stylesheet"
        />
    </head>
    <body>
        <main class="instructions-page">
            <h1>How To Use These Cards</h1>
            <div class="overlay-panel">
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        These cards are designed with Pathfinder 1 in mind, but
                        can be easily adapted to other d20 systems. The cards
                        are split into crit and fumble decks, and further
                        divided by attack type. If your system does not
                        differentiate between attack types, simply choose the
                        card that best fits the situation.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Determine who draws cards. For our table, named
                        characters draw crit cards, all characters draw fumble
                        cards.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Roll your attack as normal and confirm the crit or
                        fumble according to your table rules. Our table does not
                        confirm.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Pick the card that matches your attack type, for natural
                        attacks, choose the damage type that best fits. If your
                        weapon does multiple types of damage, you can choose.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Subtract <kbd>x1</kbd> from regular crit damage and apply
                        what the card says. Meaning <kbd>x2</kbd> => <kbd
                            >x1</kbd
                        > dmg + card, <kbd>x3</kbd> => <kbd>x2</kbd> dmg + card, <kbd
                            >x4</kbd
                        > => <kbd>x3</kbd> dmg + card, etc.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        When in doubt, GM ruling and campaign-specific house
                        rules always take priority.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Have fun! If you have a good suggestion for a card, or
                        want to share how you use them at your table, reach out
                        on <a href="https://github.com/bart-sysf/pf-crit-fumble"
                            >GitHub</a
                        >!
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <a class="btn-home" href="/">Back To Decks</a>
        </main>

        <style>
            * {
                margin: 0;
                padding: 0;
                box-sizing: border-box;
            }

            body {
                font-family: "Crimson Text", Georgia, serif;
                background: #1a1a2e url("/images/bg.png") center center / cover
                    no-repeat fixed;
                color: #f0e6d2;
                margin: 0;
                min-height: 100vh;
            }

            body::before {
                content: "";
                position: fixed;
                inset: 0;
                background: rgba(10, 10, 20, 0.65);
                z-index: 0;
            }

            .instructions-page {
                position: relative;
                z-index: 1;
                width: 100%;
                max-width: 900px;
                margin: 0 auto;
                min-height: 100vh;
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                justify-content: center;
                align-items: center;
                padding: 2rem;
                gap: 1.25rem;
            }

            h1 {
                font-family: "MedievalSharp", cursive;
                font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.2rem);
                text-align: center;
                text-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
            }

            .overlay-panel {
                width: min(100%, 760px);
                background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78);
                border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
                border-radius: 12px;
                padding: 1.4rem 1.6rem;
                color: #2d1f15;
                box-shadow: 0 16px 34px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.32);
            }

            ul {
                padding-left: 1.25rem;
                display: grid;
                gap: 0.6rem;
                font-size: 1.1rem;
                line-height: 1.45;
            }

            .btn-home {
                font-family: "MedievalSharp", cursive;
                font-size: 1.05rem;
                padding: 0.55rem 1.4rem;
                background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
                color: #f0e6d2;
                border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.45);
                border-radius: 8px;
                text-decoration: none;
                transition:
                    background 0.2s ease,
                    transform 0.2s ease;
            }

            .btn-home:hover {
                background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.32);
                transform: translateY(-2px);
            }

            @media (max-width: 600px) {
                .instructions-page {
                    padding: 1.2rem;
                }

                .overlay-panel {
                    padding: 1rem 1rem 1rem 1.1rem;
                }

                ul {
                    font-size: 1rem;
                }
            }
        </style>
    </body>
</html>
